According to RDC 406/2020, the following activities must be described in Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) or other equivalent documents:

*   Collection, processing, coding, classification, evaluation, and notification to the competent health authority [RDC 406/2020, Art. 24, § 2, I];
*   Regular analysis process to capture adverse event information from scientific literature, systematic reviews, or reference databases [RDC 406/2020, Art. 24, § 2, II];
*   Follow-up procedures for notifications without known clinical evolution [RDC 406/2020, Art. 24, § 2, III];
*   Process for detecting duplicate notifications [RDC 406/2020, Art. 24, § 2, IV];
*   Process for developing and implementing a Risk Management Plan [RDC 406/2020, Art. 24, § 2, V];
*   Process for developing Periodic Benefit-Risk Evaluation Reports [RDC 406/2020, Art. 24, § 2, VI];
*   Pharmacovigilance self-inspection procedures [RDC 406/2020, Art. 24, § 2, VII];
*   Personnel training [RDC 406/2020, Art. 24, § 2, VIII];
*   Document management [RDC 406/2020, Art. 24, § 2, IX];
*   Signal detection and review [RDC 406/2020, Art. 24, § 2, X];
*   Benefit-Risk evaluation [RDC 406/2020, Art. 24, § 2, XI];
*   Interaction between safety issues and quality deviations [RDC 406/2020, Art. 24, § 2, XII];
*   Process for responding to health authority requirements [RDC 406/2020, Art. 24, § 2, XIII];
*   Management of urgent safety information [RDC 406/2020, Art. 24, § 2, XIV];
*   Management and use of databases and other electronic systems [RDC 406/2020, Art. 24, § 2, XV]; and
*   Management of Corrective and Preventive Actions [RDC 406/2020, Art. 24, § 2, XVI].

This list is not exhaustive, and the Marketing Authorization Holder must evaluate the need to create supplementary documents for other activities [RDC 406/2020, Art. 24, § 3].

